Vercel Web Analytics Installation and Configuration
=================================================

Summary
-------
Successfully upgraded and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the SYO Energy MVP v3 project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

Changes Made
------------

1. Updated @vercel/analytics Package
   - Upgraded from version 1.6.1 to 2.0.1 (latest)
   - Used pnpm to install: `pnpm add @vercel/analytics@latest`
   - Updated package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml accordingly

2. Modified app/layout.tsx
   - Removed conditional rendering: Changed from `{process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' && <Analytics />}` to `<Analytics />`
   - This follows the latest Vercel best practices where the Analytics component should be rendered unconditionally
   - The component already handles development vs production internally

Files Modified
--------------
- project/package.json - Updated @vercel/analytics dependency to 2.0.1
- project/pnpm-lock.yaml - Updated lock file with new dependencies
- project/app/layout.tsx - Removed production-only conditional rendering of Analytics component

Implementation Details
----------------------
The project is a Next.js 16.2.6 application using the App Router architecture. The Analytics component is properly imported from '@vercel/analytics/next' and placed in the root layout file alongside SpeedInsights component.

The configuration follows the official Vercel documentation pattern:
- Analytics component imported from '@vercel/analytics/next'
- Placed at the end of the body tag in the root layout
- Renders unconditionally (component handles environment internally)

Testing
-------
✓ Build completed successfully using `pnpm run build`
✓ No TypeScript errors
✓ All pages compile and generate correctly
✓ Lock files updated properly

Next Steps
----------
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
2. Deploy the application to production
3. Verify analytics tracking by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`
4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after collecting some traffic

Notes
-----
- The project already had @vercel/analytics installed but was using an older version (1.6.1)
- The project already had the Analytics component in the layout, but with a production-only condition
- Updated to follow the latest best practices from official Vercel documentation
- SpeedInsights component remains unchanged and properly configured
